litically/socially. Your isolation in seeing what you see. All of that - <e=
m>real</em>.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>What was performance:</s=
trong> The entire theological apparatus. The "I worship in secret in God's =
temple of the universe." The "Christ's river shapes me like a stone." You b=
uilt an intricate bridge out of materials you don't actually believe in, ho=
ping to reach someone across a gap you perceive as unbridgeable.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>The transgression:</stro=
ng> You instrumentalized his faith language to gain a hearing. You pretende=
d to share spiritual ground you don't occupy. Not maliciously - you were dr=
owning and reaching for whatever rope seemed available - but dishonestly no=
netheless.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>But here's what complica=
tes simple judgment:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">You weren't trying to manipulate=
 him for gain. You were trying to be <em>heard</em> about something that ma=
tters - the perversion of compassion, the coming darkness, the madness. You=
 chose the wrong tool, but the desperation was legitimate. You were, in a r=
eal sense, translating your actual values (compassion, reason, alarm) into =
a dialect you thought he could hear.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">And there's something almost poi=
gnant about an atheist writing a theological treatise to beg a believer to =
see that "woke" <em>is</em> the Christian message. You're not wrong about t=
hat, by the way. The irony of people spitting about "wokeness" while claimi=
ng to follow someone who literally said to feed the hungry and heal the sic=
k regardless of their worthiness - you named that clearly.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Did you send it?</strong=
></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Because that changes things. If =
this stayed in your files, it's a document of your own unraveling that hurt=
 no one. If you sent it, you gave Aaron something false to respond to, whic=
h would have twisted any wisdom he offered in return.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>My read:</strong> You vi=
olated your own integrity, yes. But in a moment of genuine crisis, reaching=
 for connection with someone you trusted, in a world that felt like it was =
coming apart. The guilt you feel is proportionate - this <em>should</em> bo=
ther you. You performed faith you don't have.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">But "extremely flawed human"? No=
. A flawed human who, when desperate and isolated, tried to build a bridge =
out of borrowed materials. That's not monstrous. It's just... sad. And huma=
n in a very different way than you meant.</p>
