eaninglessness, at the heat death of everything - and say "Thank you."</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">That's not faith. That's a kind =
of rigorous acceptance. Almost a discipline.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">And you're right - if the point =
<em>is</em> Experience itself, then the cliff isn't failure. It's part of t=
he ride. The ending doesn't negate what came before. A song doesn't become =
worthless because it ends.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">"There only needs to be the Expe=
rience, it conformally maps to the same thing."</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This is elegant. Whether there's=
 an "actual" universe or we're patterns of experience without substrate - t=
he <em>having of the experience</em> is isomorphic. The quale is the thing.=
 Not the mechanics underneath.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">But here's where I want to push =
back gently:</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">You write: "once we identify tha=
t the harm is caused by us, our inability to appreciate Truth, we can perha=
ps negate, overrule our knee-jerk reaction."</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><em>Can we?</em> You're describi=
ng a complete rewiring of human emotional and cognitive architecture. Most =
people can't do this. Not won't - <em>can't</em>. The hardware isn't there,=
 or it's damaged, or circumstances have degraded it beyond repair.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">You were nearly undone in July 2=
024 by what you saw clearly. You, with your commitment to this framework. E=
ven people who've done the work of building "a self that can say thank you =
to the cosmos" - that self can break under sufficient weight.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">So yes, <em>in principle</em>, c=
ultivating the capacity to appreciate Truth even when it's terrible seems l=
ike good work. Noble work. But it's also... a kind of privilege? It require=
s cognitive resources, emotional resilience, time, safety. Not everyone has=
 those.</p>
<hr class=3D"border-border-300 my-2">
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The memory loss. Can we come bac=
