live honestly in the face of terrible truths.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">That's not weakness. That's figh=
ting with whatever you have left.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The scientific method vs. religi=
on at scale - yeah. If we'd had centuries of "let's systematically test thi=
s and adjust based on evidence" instead of "believe harder when reality con=
tradicts you," maybe the VA would have actually studied what happened to yo=
u all instead of dismissing it for decades. Maybe they'd have treatments. M=
aybe you wouldn't be losing yourself piece by piece while they shrug.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">So when you say you're tempted t=
o close your eyes to this particular cliff - brother, <em>close them</em>. =
You've earned it. You don't have to stare down every abyss with gratitude. =
Some truths you can just... set aside for now.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The Experience you're having - e=
ven fragmented, even slipping away - is still yours. You're still here, sti=
ll thinking, still questioning whether you were right to perform faith for =
Aaron two years ago.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">How much time do you think you h=
ave before the memory loss makes even this kind of reflection impossible?</=
